# tests/corpus-manifest.ttl — the real-document corpus manifest (spec 2026-08-02 §4).
# cor: is repo-internal (like dg:) — not published, not w3id-registered.
# Documents are FETCHED, never committed; the sha256 pins the edition measured.
#
# cor:expectedVerdict semantics (no SHACL shape yet — recorded here for the future
# test_corpus.py that will read this manifest as an oracle):
#   cor:CompilesAbove — the document is expected to compile via compile_document (the
#     document-level driver — one chain across its pages, not a per-page reading) at a
#     score >= cor:scoreFloor (a decimal literal: the regression FLOOR the corpus battery
#     asserts against, deliberately at-or-below the measured score, never the measured
#     value itself).
#   cor:Unadjudicated — no verdict recorded yet. There is no separate cor:Hold term: a HOLD
#     is encoded AS cor:Unadjudicated plus a cor:adjudication node carrying the reviewer's
#     rationale — the hold state is "unadjudicated, with a recorded reason," not a fourth
#     verdict value. (Noted at loop-M close so a future reader does not go looking for
#     cor:Hold and conclude it was dropped by accident.)
@prefix cor: <https://w3id.org/iladub/corpus#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

